Article 2 (Matters Covered by Surveys on Women's Economic Activities, etc.)
(1) A survey on women's economic activities (hereinafter referred to as a "fact-finding survey") conducted by the Minister of Gender Equality and Family pursuant to Article 8 (1) of the Act on the Promotion of Economic Activities and Prevention of Career Interruption of Women (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall include the following matters: [Amended on October 1, 2025.]
1. Matters concerning the employment status of women;
2. Matters concerning the working conditions and work environment of women;
3. Matters concerning the characteristics of women, etc. whose careers have been interrupted;
4. Matters concerning the job-seeking activities and vocational education and training of women, etc. whose careers have been interrupted;
5. Matters concerning the desire of women, etc. whose careers have been interrupted to participate in economic activities;
6. Other matters that the Minister of Gender Equality and Family deems necessary for promoting women's economic activities and preventing career interruption, in addition to those prescribed in subparagraphs 1 through 5.
(2) Fact-finding surveys shall be conducted regularly at three-year intervals.
(3) Fact-finding surveys may be conducted by on-site surveys, postal surveys, or methods using information and communications networks or electronic mail.
(4) Where an additional survey is necessary due to rapid changes in the social environment or other circumstances, the Minister of Gender Equality and Family may conduct an ad hoc survey to supplement a fact-finding survey. [Amended on October 1, 2025.]
